    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341-a1">

                <pb facs="0277" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg205"/>

                <p>At a meeting of the municipal council of the city of Dublin, held in the council
                    chamber, City Hall, Cork Hill, upon Monday the 1st day of May, 1865, the right
                    honorable the lord mayor in the chair—</p>
                <p>It was moved by Councillor Warren, seconded by Councillor Draper, and—</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Unanimously resolved</hi>, That we offer the expression
                    of our condolence and sympathy to the widow and family of the lamented President
                    Lincoln, in their sad bereavement.</p>
                <closer>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal</hi>.] <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>JAMES BARRINGTON, <hi rendition="#italic">Lord Mayor</hi>.</item>
                            <item>W. J. HENRY, <hi rendition="#italic">Town Clerk</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
